## What the MIT licence above does not cover

The grant above is for **the code in this repository**. It is not a grant over the game
content this code displays, because that content is not the author's to license:

- **Supercell's assets.** The league badges, the clan and player label icons, the clan
  badges, and the sixty event-card pictures are Clash of Clans art. They are used under
  Supercell's Fan Content Policy <https://supercell.com/en/fan-content-policy/> or not at
  all. Clash of Clans is a trademark of Supercell Oy; this project is unofficial and not
  endorsed by Supercell.
- **The community wiki's images.** The troop, spell, hero, hero-equipment and Town Hall
  art comes from the Clash of Clans Wiki, whose *text* is CC BY-SA. That licence does not
  extend to those images: they are user-uploaded game rips, so they remain Supercell's.
  Crediting the wiki as the source — which the app's footer does — is honest attribution,
  not a licence, and no licence to them is available to give.

**This repository redistributes none of it.** `web/public/coc/` is gitignored as a
licensing decision, so a clone carries no Supercell asset and obtains no rights to one;
the fetch scripts pull the art onto the host at deploy time. Adding the art to the repo
would not grant any rights either, and would forfeit the reason it is absent.

The full account — which asset arrives from where, what the Fan Content Policy requires of
a publicly hosted deployment, and why the wiki's text licence stops at its text — is in
[docs/game-art.md](docs/game-art.md), under
[Licensing, and why it matters more now](docs/game-art.md#licensing-and-why-it-matters-more-now).
